es_capsule","belief_state_process_reward_replay","bounded_autonomy_campaign_packet","bridge_phase_continuity_runtime","cognitive_operator_registry","cold_reader_route_map","concurrency_mission_control","engine_room_demo","formal_evidence_cell_anchor_resolver","formal_math_premise_retrieval","formal_math_readiness_gate","formal_math_verifier_trace_repair_loop","lean_std_premise_index","materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","mechanistic_interpretability_circuit_attribution_replay","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","prediction_oracle_reconciliation","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","provider_context_recipe_budget_policy","public_reveal_walkthrough","research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","routing_anti_patterns_registry","self_ignorance_coverage_ledger","semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","tool_server_pressure_inventory","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","voice_to_doctrine_self_improvement_loop","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":[],"id":"P-2","kind":"principle","plain":"A claim may say no more than the named checker, validator, registry or witness route actually computes. If the checker decides only a local contract, describe the result as that local contract and nothing wider.","principles":[],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The blood test covers one measurement only; it leaves out how several checks combine, where the overall result is as weak as the weakest of them.","maps":[{"analogy":"the iron test only supports a statement about iron","doctrine":"the claim's strength is limited to what the named check decides"},{"analogy":"writing 'perfectly healthy' after one narrow blood test","doctrine":"wording that reaches past the check to the whole system"}],"text":"A blood test for iron tells you about iron levels. It gives you no grounds to write 'in perfect health' on the chart."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A component checks that a result record has the expected fields, and a summary page treats that field check as evidence that the underlying property holds everywhere.","does_not_prove":"Capping a claim at what its checker computes does nothing to make a weak checker stronger.","enforced_in_component_ids":["formal_math_readiness_gate","batch12_release_claim_language_gate","agent_route_observability_runtime"],"example":{"component_ids":["formal_math_readiness_gate"],"text":"The formal-math readiness gate computes how far its available evidence reaches and reports only that much, so a local check is never written up as overall readiness."},"governs":"How strong a claim may be, given the check that accepted it.","plain":"A statement can only be as strong as the exact thing the check settled. If a check confirms one small, local fact, the writing around it must stay at that size.","potential_misread":"That because the underlying check was real, any confident sentence built on it is also safe, when the sentence can only claim what the check decided.","refuses":"Using a checker that decides one local contract to support wording about the whole system.","requires":"Limiting each claim to what its named checker, validator, registry or witness route actually computes, with the limit computed from the underlying obligations.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"It keeps a narrow, real check from being written up as a broad claim, so readers can see what was actually tested."},"rests_on":["AX-1","AX-5"],"source_ref":"PRINCIPLES.md::P-2","statement":"Grounding: AX-1, AX-5.\nObligation grounding: AX-1.O1.certificate_exists, AX-1.O2.checker_accepts, AX-1.O3.claim_ceiling, AX-1.O4.bare_assertion_bottom, AX-5.O1.composite_status_meets_parts, AX-5.O2.no_evidence_defaults_blocked, AX-5.O3.authority_cannot_raise_without_derivation.\n\nA claim may say no more than the named checker, validator, registry or witness\nroute actually computes. If the checker decides only a local contract, describe\nthe result as that local contract and nothing wider.","statement_sha256":"92b9b7da4a5beae365fb1a807310643b830367ebf39974c186345296de4d7ba1","title":"Lower claim strength to checker strength","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}